139535942 true] [17592186375527 1113 #uuid "c5a2285c-007a-5c4d-b1d4-af08d8caa89a" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375527 1145 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $2$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+10\\cdot {M}_{21} \\\\  & =2{M}_{11}+10{M}_{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375529 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375530 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375531 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375532 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375533 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1041 "selection" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375529 13194139535942 true] [17592186375528 1110 #uuid "840f6e9f-cfe7-5fe4-91f4-4781f047355b" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375529 1034 "2{M}_{11}+10{M}_{21}" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375529 1111 #uuid "9c3675c4-f868-515a-8eff-8b5cba5d07a9" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375530 1034 "10{M}_{11}+2{M}_{21}" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375530 1111 #uuid "3d8c2c3b-08cf-5d37-945d-b944dcf5f1c7" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375531 1034 "{M}_{11}+5{M}_{21}" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375531 1111 #uuid "f1a106c5-f3b8-5178-b18c-f3a1d7d40e9f" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375532 1034 "{M}_{11}+{M}_{21}" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375532 1111 #uuid "36a831ed-1c52-532b-94d5-0171b12a603f" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375533 1034 "20{M}_{11}\\cdot {M}_{21}" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375533 1111 #uuid "443bc837-3151-567a-8574-996a2c74437b" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375535 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1089 "q-123132" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1100 "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [1,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=xy.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,3,5,7},\\,{P}_{2}={1,6},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1113 #uuid "173dae7c-03a9-58e0-bb98-2869b614756e" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375534 1145 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072318/assets/68270610704b1ef132469193e7948f54e548fa22223b6fc49b693753f998f874.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=10$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10\\cdot {M}_{11}+10\\cdot {M}_{21}+10\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =10({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=xy$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=xy$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072318/assets/7611c64cc460db725893156f6043644b34962a04f2aacef0b19cf99c5769cda3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072318/assets/75f378700ce6593a7ed9577b34e093cbbfe702e9512e9962e0d6f7f681694842.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(3,6)=18 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(5,6)=30 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(7,6)=42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10(18+30+42) \\\\  & =900.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375536 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375537 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375538 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375539 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375540 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1041 "selection" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375536 13194139535942 true] [17592186375535 1110 #uuid "884dab17-71e2-5757-adb9-19776e524395" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375536 1034 "900" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375536 1111 #uuid "8b17d64e-c3a2-5fa0-9f7d-e604d552cb36" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375537 1034 "320" 13194139535942 true] [17592186375537 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535942 true] [17592186375537 1111 #uuid "e53